# �T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T
# BOS Pipeline v9.0 �� Celery Worker Dockerfile
# Shared base with the API, different entrypoint
# �T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T�T

# ���� Stage 1: Builder ����
FROM python:3.11-slim AS builder

WORKDIR /build

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    gcc \
    libpq-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --prefix=/install -r requirements.txt

# ���� Stage 2: Runtime ����
FROM python:3.11-slim AS runtime

LABEL maintainer="BOS Pipeline Team"
LABEL version="9.0.0"
LABEL description="BOS Pipeline Celery Worker"

RUN groupadd -r bos && useradd -r -g bos -d /app -s /sbin/nologin bos

WORKDIR /app

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    libpq5 \
    curl \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY --from=builder /install /usr/local
COPY . .
RUN chown -R bos:bos /app

USER bos

# Health check: verify Celery is responsive
HEALTHCHECK --interval=60s --timeout=15s --start-period=30s --retries=3 \
    CMD celery -A app.celery_app:celery_app inspect ping --timeout 10 || exit 1

# Default: start worker listening on all queues
CMD ["celery", "-A", "app.celery_app:celery_app", "worker", \
     "--loglevel=info", \
     "--concurrency=4", \
     "--queues=default,compute,export,webhook,maintenance", \
     "--max-tasks-per-child=200", \
     "-n", "worker@%h"]
